These run script templates are dedicated to code for generating the Hamiltonian for a {p, 3} hyperbolic lattice
with external uniform axial magnetic field (parameterized by qaxial, see below) and obtaining the DOS of the Hamiltonian
from utilization of the kernel polynomial method (KPM).

General conventions:
pval is p in {p, 3} appearing in the Schlafli symbol for hyperbolic lattices (q always assumed to be =3)
nval is the number of generations (unlike in the paper, in the code we start counting from 1 not 0)
qaxial parameterizes the strength of the uniform axial magnetic field
Nm is the number of moments to compute in the Chebyshev polynomial expansion in KPM

Note that since KPM requires rescaling of the Hamiltonian, bounds of the eigenspectrum must be given.
Exact bounds could be computed via Lanczos algorithm, however it is more efficient to statically set these
bounds here to some static value. For zero axial field [-3.12, 3.12] will work fine. For nonzero
magnitudes of the axial field (qaxial), a larger window may be needed due to band broadening.
